From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:39:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 63/72] deepseek: keep a replicated mirror of each slot's first
 compressed KV rows (TF_DSV41_KV_MIRROR)

TF_DSV41_KV_MIRROR=<positions> keeps each slot's first compressed KV rows
whole on every rank. Split KV stays on. A window whose program ends at or
before the mirror reads it instead of exchanging rows, so the split-KV
exchange (kx_dense / kx_union) and its early path are skipped. The
condition uses the program's end (a graph bucket's end, or the replicated
slot position for an eager window). Every rank decides alike, and no graph
key, capture or bucket is added.

Each compressed _kv_store (decode and prefill compress) is followed by a
second store of the same rows into the mirror. Rows past the mirror go to a
discard page. The store runs in every window while the knob is on, because
row mode mixes slots. Session restores fill the mirror after syncTables:
each rank gathers its owned rows, then an all-gather fills the slot's run.
The rows are the same bytes as split KV's exchanged rows, read in the same
entry order, so attention gives the same bits. Values round up to page
times world. Setting it without KV split is refused. The boot check counts
the mirror's bytes, and rank 0 logs them.

Unset or 0 emits what H emits and allocates nothing. Host tests cover the
knob, the layout, the fill and the emitted programs on and off.
`tf-dsv41-test kv-mirror` compares attention through the mirror with split
KV's exchanged rows on a GPU.

Mechanism after Bertholomus's dsv41 replicated compressed-KV plane
(model.zig), re-implemented here in bounded form; credited in docs/credits.md.

Co-authored-by: bertholomus <311723197+bertholomus@users.noreply.github.com>
